  "result": "I've found earlier tickets asking for the same thing, so I'm sending the final answer now.\n\n{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#21981\", \"PowerToys#27413\"], \"answer\": \"This has been requested before. PowerToys#21981 asks for a setting to turn off the \\\"What's New\\\" window after an update. PowerToys#27413 asks for a settings toggle plus a group policy to turn off the \\\"Whats new\\\" popup. The maintainer's last comment on #27413 says it is included in v0.78.0. The comment doesn't say whether that covers the group policy, the per-user setting, or both. Update to the latest PowerToys and look in Settings for an option to turn off the post-update What's New popup. If you manage several machines, check the PowerToys group policy templates for a matching policy. The archive doesn't mention a \\\"Don't show again\\\" checkbox in the popup or a badge on the What's New button. If you still want those, add your use case to the existing tickets.\"}",
